<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#etsu-nupe">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Etsu Nupe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Etsu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nupe-kingdom">Nupe</a> is the title of the traditional ruler of the Nupe people of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> conquest of Nupe in the 19th century, the title has been held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> of the dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallam-dendo">Mallam Dendo</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bida">Bida</a>. The Etsu Nupe kept his position under British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indirect-rule">indirect rule</a> and remains an important traditional authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/etsu-nupe.jpg" alt="Etsu Nupe" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JelaniZ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Place_of_Etsue_Nupe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
